 "notes": "Stretch 1: p.123 from the title 'ṭua Rā em uben - f em χut' (row 1, below the rule) to 'nefer-θà em' at its foot; p.124 all nine rows to 'ṭua - k pautti χeperu uṭ χeru ta'. Plate: p.123 rows 1-2 = XVIII; heading 'PLATE XIX.' after row 2; all later words XIX. Line numerals: p.123 '1.' at the head of row 1 before ṭua; '2.' in row 2 before Rā (after ànet' - ḥrà - k); '3.' in row 4 inside χu (after G25 Aa1); '4.' in row 5 inside āṭtet (before X1 X1 + boat); '5.' in row 7 inside hennu - nek (after O4 N35); '6.' in row 8 before ḥetep. p.124 '7.' in row 2 before Tem; '8.' in row 3 before neteru; '9.' in row 5 inside 'Ṭes Ṭes' (before the final canal N36); '10.' in row 7 before nefer; '11.' in row 9 inside ṭua - k (before V31). Last numeral on p.124 = 11. Overlines: only on p.123. Row 1 has three separate short overlines: over ṭua only; over em uben - f em (Rā and χut are NOT under a line); over er χeper ḥetep - f em. Row 2: one overline from the row start over ānχ t'eṭ àn, ending before Àusàr. No overlines on p.124 or on p.123 rows 3-8. No square brackets anywhere in the hieroglyph lines; brackets only in Budge's English ([when], [thy], [my], [as], [thou], [The gods of], [and]) and in his transliteration 'nemà - [k]' (no k sign printed). No footnotes, no Appendix. Word division follows Budge's spaced groups except 'Ḥeru χuti' kept as one name; 'mer Ṭes Ṭes' split mer / Ṭes Ṭes; 'Tem' separate. The braided column with splayed foot (net'em, seku, ḥept, seḥeq, sek - nes) is the same type shape throughout; coded V28 (approx where V29/M29 expected)."
